      phase 1 (approach): 0+ diagonal-forward steps toward obstacle from root side (FL if root is left, FR if right)
      phase 2 (alongside): 0+ straight-forward steps running alongside obstacle
      phase 3 (exit): 0+ diagonal-forward steps away on the opposite side (FR if phase1 was FL, vice versa)
      lengths of three phases roughly balanced (eval avg: ~ 2:1:2)
    no backward or lateral steps; phase transitions are strictly monotone (no mixing)
    segment does not pass through obstacle
    pixel count preserved (truncated if route hits grid boundary)
  colors: 3 per triple (all distinct within triple); bg is most-frequent color

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size N (7-27), bg color, number of triples T (1-3)
    2. For each triple, place bar perpendicular to a chosen border edge with length 3-7
    3. Draw output segment path (length L, 5-9) from bar terminal attach point with 3 monotone phases: diagonal-forward approach on root side (FL* or FR*, matching which side of bar the root is on), straight-forward alongside (F*), diagonal-forward exit on opposite side; lengths of three phases roughly balanced (eval avg: ~ 2:1:2); 
    4. Place obstacle sprite (1-9 px, irregular shape) inside the concavity, touching the V apex on its inner side; grow from the apex inward; manhattan distance 2-6 from bar terminal
    5. Build the output grid with bars, output segments, and obstacles
    6. Derive input: translate the output segment path backward (toward border, away from obstacle) so it extends in the opposite forward-direction from the obstacle; reshape into an irregular 8-connected stroke of same length L; input segment must not be 4-adjacent to obstacle
    7. Validate no overlaps between components and segment does not touch obstacle in input

